WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.250
Let's take a look at Teams and Admin in
Macro.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.315
When your team shares a task, a document,
or a customer record, you can see who can

00:00:08.315 --> 00:00:10.267
open it right where the work happens.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.890
Open Settings, then Team.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.700
Click Create Team, give it a name, and add
the first people.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.290
Once the team's set up, go to Members.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.960
Here you can invite someone by email and
check who has accepted.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:35.467
For a pending invite, copy the invite link
to send it directly.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:46.050
There are two invite settings. Turn off
Members can invite to limit invitations to

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.650
admins and the owner.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:53.875
Turn on Auto-join on domain if you want new
sign-ups from your company's email domain

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:55.120
to join automatically.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.700
You can switch back to invite-only any
time.

00:01:00.077 --> 00:01:03.317
Members can open work that's shared with
the team.

00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:08.587
Admins can manage invites, remove members,
and manage the CRM.

00:01:08.587 --> 00:01:10.937
The owner can change people's roles.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.833
Removing a member takes away their team
access.

00:01:17.897 --> 00:01:20.507
Let's open a doc called Launch Plan.

00:01:20.507 --> 00:01:22.427
A new doc is private.

00:01:22.427 --> 00:01:23.597
Click Share.

00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:32.402
Choose a person or channel, and pick Can
view, Can comment, or Can edit. To share

00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:35.263
with the whole team, use Team Access.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:43.161
You can change access later in the same
dialog. Keep the link restricted to people

00:01:43.161 --> 00:01:48.600
with access or widen it to the team or
anyone with the link when you need to.

00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:53.473
If you mention that doc in a channel,

00:01:53.473 --> 00:01:55.793
the people in the channel can open it.

00:01:55.793 --> 00:01:59.303
Teammates who join later get that context
too.

00:01:59.303 --> 00:02:03.233
When someone leaves, they lose the access
that channel gave them.

00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:09.743
Tasks work a little differently.

00:02:09.743 --> 00:02:15.023
When you're on a team, the team-sharing
switch starts on in the task composer.

00:02:15.023 --> 00:02:17.313
So for Send the onboarding checklist,

00:02:17.313 --> 00:02:20.667
I'll leave it on and the team can open it
right away.

00:02:23.933 --> 00:02:25.683
For a personal reminder,

00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:28.467
turn it off before you create the task.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.360
Now open Customers.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.130
On a company record,

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:41.922
open Email contribution settings to see
whether your mailbox shares with the CRM

00:02:41.922 --> 00:02:44.067
and which domains are excluded.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:52.367
Admins can archive a company to take it out
of the team's active lists and keep its history.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.150
A pipeline starts private.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.467
Turn on team sharing if you want to work on
it together.

00:03:08.393 --> 00:03:14.223
Calls in team channels share the recording
and transcript with the team by default.

00:03:14.223 --> 00:03:17.663
Private channels and direct messages start
private.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.563
You can change sharing during the call.

00:03:20.563 --> 00:03:27.100
Shared work gives your agents team context
within the access they already have.

00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:31.693
And that's it.

00:03:31.693 --> 00:03:37.945
Set up the team in Settings, and open Share
whenever you want to check who can open

00:03:37.945 --> 00:03:38.313
something.
